1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,090
A book scanner's brochure resolution tells you very little.

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:11,550
Archives that follow FADGI judge scanners by measured image quality at a defined star level, not by a single dpi figure.

3
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:23,140
FADGI, the US Federal Agencies Digital Guidelines Initiative, publishes technical guidelines for digitising cultural heritage materials.

4
00:00:23,490 --> 00:00:30,020
Its third edition was published on 10 May 2023, after editions in 2010 and 2016.

5
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:35,750
The four star levels grade the images a system produces, not the scanner alone.

6
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:41,860
Several criteria are measured, and file format and colour space are set for each level.

7
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:54,110
Many institutions also use ISO/TS 19264-1, the international specification for reflective originals such as books, documents and prints.

8
00:00:54,610 --> 00:01:07,560
Before you buy, ask which star level your project needs, ask for measured results on material like yours, and check calibration, cradle protection for fragile bindings, and operator training.

9
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:13,780
